        <technology>
            <technologyDescriptionAndIncludedProcesses xml:lang="en">This dataset includes a method of producing a seperator for a lithium ion battery. The seperator seperates anode from cathode, but allows an exchange of Li+-ions through micropores. In case of to high process temperature of the battery, the seperator melts, thus closes the micopores, interrupts the Li+-ion exchange and therefore stops the chemical process and pretends finally from overheating or a burning battery .\n\n# Included processes\nThis dataset incudes the production of a seperator for a lithium-ion battery. Polyethylene foil is coated with a slurry composed of silica, a Co-polymere of PVDF (proxy: PVF) and hexafluor ethane and dibutyl phthalate (proxy: phthalic anhydride). The polytehylene foil is coated on 1 side with the slurry. Then, the coated foil is dried in a "dry channel" (H2O content &lt; 20 ppm) and coiled up. The same procedure is done for the second side of the collector foil.</technologyDescriptionAndIncludedProcesses>
        </technology>
    </processInformation>
